  "top10": {
    "totalFound": 10,
    "introHtml": "<p>The best convertibles across all three sources, ranked by overall value: price vs. mileage, deal ratings, accident history, and driving character. Great Deals and no-accident flags were heavily weighted.</p>",
    "picks": [
      {"rank":1,"year":2011,"make":"BMW","model":"3 Series","trim":"328i","price":7489,"mileage":89795,"location":"Medford, NJ","distanceMi":null,"url":"https://www.cargurus.com/details/458428863","dealer":null,"dealRating":"Great Deal","cleanTitle":null,"noAccidents":null,"transmission":"Automatic","imageUrl":null,"source":"cargurus","whyGood":"CarGurus flagged this as a Great Deal — 2011 328i with 89K miles at $7,489 is significantly under market. The 3 Series convertible (E93) is a proven, durable platform known for longevity past 150K with routine maintenance.","whatToVerify":"Check for rust on the convertible top frame and around wheel arches. Confirm the folding roof mechanism operates smoothly. Pull a full Carfax. Have a BMW-familiar shop inspect the cooling system and valve cover gasket.","bottomLine":"Best price-to-value in the entire list. If the inspection checks out, this is an easy buy."},
      {"rank":2,"year":2008,"make":"BMW","model":"1 Series","trim":"135i","price":11595,"mileage":48371,"location":"Turnersville, NJ","distanceMi":null,"url":"https://www.cargurus.com/details/458097611","dealer":null,"dealRating":"Good Deal","cleanTitle":null,"noAccidents":null,"transmission":"Manual","imageUrl":null,"source":"cargurus","whyGood":"Only 48,371 miles on a twin-turbo 300hp inline-6 — exceptional for a 2008 model. The 135i is a drivers' car with a rabid enthusiast community and strong aftermarket support. Manual transmission adds to the appeal. Good Deal badge confirms it's priced below market.","whatToVerify":"The N54 engine is known for injector and high-pressure fuel pump wear — have both inspected. Check the charge pipes for cracks. Confirm the convertible roof electronics work properly.","bottomLine":"The lowest-mileage car in this entire search by a wide margin. For a driving enthusiast, this is the hidden gem of the list."},
      {"rank":3,"year":2016,"make":"Volkswagen","model":"Beetle","trim":"Denim","price":11875,"mileage":98000,"location":null,"distanceMi":null,"url":"https://www.autotrader.com/cars-for-sale/vehicle/793295641","dealer":"Private Seller","dealRating":null,"cleanTitle":true,"noAccidents":true,"transmission":"Automatic","imageUrl":"https://images2.autotrader.com/scaler/408/306/ps-vehicle-media/0b28e547-b2a9-4c31-9695-3f8c9d0442e5.jpeg","source":"autotrader","whyGood":"Newest car in the entire search, with a verified clean title and no-accident history. The 2016 Beetle convertible with the limited-edition Denim package is rare and desirable. VW's 1.8T engine is reliable and well-supported.","whatToVerify":"Private seller — run a Carfax and have an independent pre-purchase inspection. Verify the convertible roof seals are intact. Check DSG transmission fluid service history if equipped.","bottomLine":"The safest bet if you want a modern daily driver with verified clean history. The Denim trim makes it stand out."},
      {"rank":4,"year":2013,"make":"INFINITI","model":"G37","trim":"Convertible","price":11488,"mileage":91000,"location":"Willow Grove, PA","distanceMi":21,"url":"https://www.autotrader.com/cars-for-sale/vehicle/791439500","dealer":"Faulkner INFINITI of Willow Grove","dealRating":"Great Deal","cleanTitle":null,"noAccidents":true,"transmission":"Automatic","imageUrl":"https://images2.autotrader.com/scaler/408/306/hn/c/10687f6398594b5b84e5c5000d5117ba.jpg","source":"autotrader","whyGood":"Great Deal badge plus no-accident history at a franchised INFINITI dealer — 21 miles from Media. The G37 Convertible's 328hp V6 and rear-wheel drive make it one of the most engaging cars in this price range. INFINITI dealers typically do a thorough pre-sale inspection.","whatToVerify":"Ask for the dealer inspection report. Check the folding hard-top mechanism carefully — these complex roofs can be expensive to repair. Verify the VQ37VHR engine shows no oil consumption issues.","bottomLine":"Great Deal + no accidents + dealer support = strongest combination of value and peace-of-mind in the top 4."},
      {"rank":5,"year":2004,"make":"BMW","model":"6 Series","trim":"645Ci","price":9995,"mileage":59113,"location":"West Chester, PA","distanceMi":null,"url":"https://www.cargurus.com/details/464027054","dealer":null,"dealRating":null,"cleanTitle":null,"noAccidents":null,"transmission":"Manual","imageUrl":null,"source":"cargurus","whyGood":"A manual-transmission V8 drop-top for under $10K with only 59,000 miles is extraordinary. The E64 645Ci is a grand tourer that commands attention, and the 6-speed manual version is rare. Same low mileage as the AT listing but from CarGurus for cross-reference.","whatToVerify":"The N62 V8 is known for Vanos actuator wear and valley pan gasket leaks — budget ~$500 for preventive maintenance if not already done. Have the SMG hydraulics (or manual clutch) inspected. Run a Carfax.","bottomLine":"Rare manual V8 at a price that's hard to believe. Worth a thorough PPI — the N62 quirks are well-documented and manageable."},
      {"rank":6,"year":2004,"make":"BMW","model":"6 Series","trim":"645Ci","price":10884,"mileage":59000,"location":"West Chester, PA","distanceMi":8,"url":"https://www.autotrader.com/cars-for-sale/vehicle/795975112","dealer":"Audi West Chester","dealRating":null,"cleanTitle":null,"noAccidents":true,"transmission":"Automatic","imageUrl":"https://images2.autotrader.com/scaler/408/306/hn/c/1fde3e26ba014b879277107de2c973b1.jpg","source":"autotrader","whyGood":"No-accident history, only 59K miles, and just 8 miles from Media at a franchised dealer. The automatic 645Ci is more livable daily and the same grand-touring package as the manual version at #5. Audi West Chester is a reputable dealer.","whatToVerify":"Same N62 V8 concerns as #5. Ask for the full dealer inspection report. Confirm all iDrive electronics, retractable roof, and sensors are operational.","bottomLine":"The more practical sibling of #5. With no-accident history and dealer backing, this is the cleaner buy if you prefer an automatic."},
      {"rank":7,"year":2004,"make":"Mercedes-Benz","model":"CLK","trim":"CLK500","price":7900,"mileage":82000,"location":null,"distanceMi":32,"url":"https://www.autotrader.com/cars-for-sale/vehicle/788479418","dealer":null,"dealRating":null,"cleanTitle":true,"noAccidents":true,"transmission":"Automatic","imageUrl":"https://images2.autotrader.com/scaler/408/306/ps-vehicle-media/691652ff-2b5f-401b-89c6-0ffd9a0ba397.png","source":"autotrader","whyGood":"Clean title + no accidents on a 302hp V8 Mercedes convertible at $7,900 is a remarkable value. The W208 CLK500 is a timeless design and the M113 V8 is one of Mercedes' most reliable engines — well-documented and inexpensive to service compared to more exotic platforms.","whatToVerify":"Inspect the hydraulic convertible roof system carefully — these can leak and repairs run $1,000+. Check the air suspension if equipped. Verify the instrument cluster and electronics all function.","bottomLine":"Best price per horsepower with verified clean history. The CLK500 looks and feels like a $25K car. Due diligence on the roof seals is the main homework item."},
      {"rank":8,"year":2011,"make":"Volkswagen","model":"Eos","trim":null,"price":7495,"mileage":72422,"location":"Huntingdon Valley, PA","distanceMi":null,"url":"https://www.cargurus.com/details/460058215","dealer":null,"dealRating":"Good Deal","cleanTitle":null,"noAccidents":null,"transmission":"Automatic","imageUrl":null,"source":"cargurus","whyGood":"Good Deal badge, 72K miles, and $7,495 — the Eos is criminally undervalued. It features a glass sunroof that integrates into the folding metal hardtop roof, giving you a sunroof experience even with the top up. Very practical four-seater.","whatToVerify":"The DSG transmission and the complex roof mechanism are the two things to scrutinize. Have a VW specialist check the roof seals and hydraulic lines. Confirm the DSG fluid has been serviced.","bottomLine":"Most practical convertible at this price point — real back seat, real trunk, real weather protection. Great for someone who wants a daily-driver droptop."},
      {"rank":9,"year":2012,"make":"Audi","model":"A5","trim":"2.0T","price":8495,"mileage":80410,"location":"Towamencin, PA","distanceMi":null,"url":"https://www.cars.com/vehicledetail/1faf3dba/","dealer":"Private Seller","dealRating":null,"cleanTitle":null,"noAccidents":null,"transmission":null,"imageUrl":"https://platform.cstatic-images.com/large/in/v2/p2p/16b786f6-0c39-436c-95a7-05465908b11d/01d78260-a9ec-422a-8a85-d830ecdabb8f","source":"cars.com","whyGood":"Private-seller A5 Cabriolet with Quattro AWD at $8,495 and 80K miles is well under market. The B8 A5 is a sleek, well-engineered convertible with enough luxury to feel premium without the maintenance complexity of the S5 or A8.","whatToVerify":"Private sale — Carfax and PPI are essential. The 2.0T timing chain tensioner issue (pre-2012 mostly, but verify) should be confirmed as serviced. Check the folding roof hydraulics and Quattro drivetrain operation.","bottomLine":"Solid AWD daily-driver potential at a compelling price. Private sale warrants careful due diligence, but the value here is real."},
      {"rank":10,"year":2010,"make":"Audi","model":"S5","trim":"Cabriolet","price":9999,"mileage":92034,"location":"Feasterville Trevose, PA","distanceMi":null,"url":"https://www.cargurus.com/details/459964081","dealer":null,"dealRating":"Fair Deal","cleanTitle":null,"noAccidents":null,"transmission":"Automatic","imageUrl":null,"source":"cargurus","whyGood":"The S5 Cabriolet packs a naturally-aspirated 354hp V8 — a powertrain that Audi later replaced with a less exciting turbocharged V6. This is a future classic. At $9,999 with 92K miles, it's priced fairly for what it is.","whatToVerify":"The 4.2L FSI V8 has known carbon buildup issues requiring periodic walnut blasting (~$500). The dual-clutch S-tronic should be fluid-serviced. Confirm the folding roof seals and all quattro drivetrain components.","bottomLine":"The connoisseur's pick. A V8 all-wheel-drive convertible under $10K is rare — this won't be this cheap for long."}
    ]
  },
  "manual10": {
    "totalFound": 6,
    "introHtml": "<p>Manual-transmission convertibles only — the driver's picks. Ranked by the combination of price, mileage, and the pure pleasure of rowing your own gears. All six manual cars found across all three sources are listed here.</p>",
    "picks": [
      {"rank":1,"year":2008,"make":"BMW","model":"1 Series","trim":"135i","price":11595,"mileage":48371,"location":"Turnersville, NJ","distanceMi":null,"url":"https://www.cargurus.com/details/458097611","dealer":null,"dealRating":"Good Deal","cleanTitle":null,"noAccidents":null,"transmission":"Manual","imageUrl":null,"source":"cargurus","whyGood":"Only 48K miles on a 300hp twin-turbo inline-6 with a 6-speed manual — this is the unicorn of the manual list. The 135i is a pure sports car in an unexpected package. Good Deal badge below market price.","whatToVerify":"N54 engine: check injectors, HPFP, and charge pipes. Manual clutch wear — ask for history. Confirm convertible roof hydraulics are working.","bottomLine":"The best manual car in this search, full stop. If you value the driving experience above all else, this is the one."},
      {"rank":2,"year":2004,"make":"BMW","model":"6 Series","trim":"645Ci","price":9995,"mileage":59113,"location":"West Chester, PA","distanceMi":null,"url":"https://www.cargurus.com/details/464027054","dealer":null,"dealRating":null,"cleanTitle":null,"noAccidents":null,"transmission":"Manual","imageUrl":null,"source":"cargurus","whyGood":"A 6-speed manual V8 drop-top at $9,995 is virtually impossible to find. The E64 645Ci was available with a manual only briefly, and survivors are prized by enthusiasts. Only 59K miles adds to the appeal.","whatToVerify":"N62 V8 Vanos actuators and valley pan gasket. Manual transmission fluid condition and clutch wear. Full Carfax.","bottomLine":"Rare and desirable. A proper Grand Touring machine with a stick shift — a car worth seeking out specifically."},
      {"rank":3,"year":2011,"make":"BMW","model":"3 Series","trim":"328i","price":7995,"mileage":118267,"location":"Feasterville-Trevose, PA","distanceMi":null,"url":"https://www.cargurus.com/details/462017255","dealer":null,"dealRating":"Fair Deal","cleanTitle":null,"noAccidents":null,"transmission":"Manual","imageUrl":null,"source":"cargurus","whyGood":"Manual 328i convertible under $8K is rare in this market. The E93 platform is well-proven and 118K miles on a properly maintained N52 engine is not worrying. Good bones for a fun daily driver.","whatToVerify":"VANOS seals and valve cover gasket are common wear items. Check the folding roof mechanism and convertible top seals carefully. Confirm full maintenance history.","bottomLine":"Entry-level manual BMW convertible experience at a very accessible price. Know what you're getting: fair deal pricing means limited upside but no obvious red flags."},
      {"rank":4,"year":2012,"make":"Volkswagen","model":"Eos","trim":null,"price":8999,"mileage":86370,"location":"Croydon, PA","distanceMi":null,"url":"https://www.cargurus.com/details/461597986","dealer":null,"dealRating":"Fair Deal","cleanTitle":null,"noAccidents":null,"transmission":"Manual","imageUrl":null,"source":"cargurus","whyGood":"Manual Eos with 86K miles at $8,999 is a practical four-seat hardtop convertible with a stick shift — a rarer combination than it sounds. Croydon PA is local. The Eos is underrated for real-world usability.","whatToVerify":"DSG vs 6MT — confirm it's truly manual. Inspect the folding roof mechanism thoroughly; Eos roofs are complex. Check the 2.0T timing chain (post-2010 improved tensioner but verify).","bottomLine":"The most practical manual convertible in the list — 4 seats, hardtop, real trunk. Great choice if you need daily usability plus a manual gearbox."},
      {"rank":5,"year":2010,"make":"Ford","model":"Mustang","trim":"GT","price":14495,"mileage":80750,"location":"West Chester, PA","distanceMi":null,"url":"https://www.cargurus.com/details/462882505","dealer":null,"dealRating":"Fair Deal","cleanTitle":null,"noAccidents":null,"transmission":"Manual","imageUrl":null,"source":"cargurus","whyGood":"The only manual Mustang GT in this entire search — 315hp V8 with a stick shift at the top of the budget. 80K miles is the lowest of all the Mustangs. If you want the real Mustang experience with a V8 and a stick, this is the only choice in the list.","whatToVerify":"At $14,495 it's the priciest Mustang here. Have the clutch, transmission, and all V8-specific items (cam phasers, spark plugs) inspected. Confirm the convertible top is in good shape.","bottomLine":"The enthusiast's Mustang. Pay the extra few thousand to get the real V8 manual experience — there's no other GT in this market right now."},
      {"rank":6,"year":2014,"make":"Ford","model":"Mustang","trim":"V6","price":7499,"mileage":167500,"location":"Woodlynne, NJ","distanceMi":null,"url":"https://www.cargurus.com/details/461341277","dealer":null,"dealRating":"Fair Deal","cleanTitle":null,"noAccidents":null,"transmission":"Manual","imageUrl":null,"source":"cargurus","whyGood":"Cheapest manual convertible in the entire search at $7,499. The 2014 V6 Mustang made 305hp and is mechanically simple. High miles (167K) explain the price — this is a buyer who understands cars.","whatToVerify":"With 167K miles the clutch, transmission synchros, and suspension bushings all need inspection. Pull a Carfax. Have a trusted mechanic assess the overall condition honestly.","bottomLine":"High-risk, high-reward for someone mechanically inclined. At $7,499 for a manual Mustang, there's room to absorb a repair or two and still come out ahead."}
    ]
